cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Refract in research, please cite it."
title: "Refract: a deterministic claim-provenance engine for Wikipedia page histories"
abstract: >-
  Refract reconstructs when a claim entered, changed, or left a source, and reports
  which downstream claims and citations built on a version that no longer says what
  was cited.
version: 0.5.14
date-released: 2026-07-29
authors:
  - given-names: Kanav
    family-names: Jain
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-5202-0920"
    affiliation: NextConsensus
repository-code: "https://github.com/refract-org/refract"
license: AGPL-3.0
type: software
keywords:
  - provenance
  - claim tracking
  - citation integrity
  - Wikipedia
